  {
   "id": 68837846,
   "body": "This is a well explained version of a pet-peeve-idea I got from two videos published 30 years apart:\n- 1994 Danny Hillis' TED Talk: Back to the future (of 1994): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gdg4mU-wuhI\n- 2023 Tom Scott's video: My worries about the trajectory of A.I. [relevant part 00:25 - 02:38] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jPhJbKBuNnA\n\nBoth show a sigmoid curve with a exponential-ish first half to represent progress. My take is that, not only we don't know where on the curve we are, we've been lost for (at least) the last 30 years and we've made no progress with our estimations.\n\nWe're living interesting times.",
   "body_json": {
    "type": "doc",
    "attrs": {
     "schemaVersion": "v1"
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This is a well explained version of a pet-peeve-idea I got from two videos published 30 years apart:"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "- 1994 Danny Hillis' TED Talk: Back to the future (of 1994): "
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gdg4mU-wuhI",
        "marks": [
         {
          "type": "link",
          "attrs": {
           "href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gdg4mU-wuhI"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "- 2023 Tom Scott's video: My worries about the trajectory of A.I. [relevant part 00:25 - 02:38] "
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jPhJbKBuNnA",
        "marks": [
         {
          "type": "link",
          "attrs": {
           "href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jPhJbKBuNnA"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Both show a sigmoid curve with a exponential-ish first half to represent progress. My take is that, not only we don't know where on the curve we are, we've been lost for (at least) the last 30 years and we've made no progress with our estimations."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "We're living interesting times."
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
